      "question": {
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
